@startuml
' Basic Pipe-and-Filter Architecture
' Shows the fundamental structure: Source → Transformers → Sink

!include ../../../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/structural/component-diagram-style.iuml
!include pipe-and-filter-roles.iuml

title Basic Pipe-and-Filter Architecture

[Data\nSource] <<source>> as Source
[Filter A\n(Transform)] <<transformer>> as FilterA
[Filter B\n(Transform)] <<transformer>> as FilterB
[Filter C\n(Transform)] <<transformer>> as FilterC
[Data\nSink] <<sink>> as Sink

Source -right-> FilterA : " Pipe "
FilterA -right-> FilterB : " Pipe "
FilterB -right-> FilterC : " Pipe "
FilterC -right-> Sink : " Pipe "

legend right
  |= Symbol |= Meaning |
  | <$deep_primary> | Source (Producer) |
  | <$deep_ok> | Transformer |
  | <$deep_caution> | Sink (Consumer) |
  | → | Data Flow (Pipe) |
endlegend

@enduml
